The optional Beat This backend uses the MIT-licensed `beat-this` Rust crate,
which is a port of the MIT-licensed Beat This! model by the Institute of
Computational Perception, Johannes Kepler University Linz. Model files are not
distributed by this repository. See `models/README.md` for provenance and
license requirements.

The Beat This adapter's audio decoding scaffold and sinc parameters are
adapted from beat-this-rs 1.0.0. Copyright (c) 2025 danigb (Rust port), and
Copyright (c) 2024 Institute of Computational Perception, JKU Linz, Austria
("Beat This!" original work). The retained MIT terms are in
`licenses/beat-this-rs-MIT.txt`.

The optional evaluation submodule at
`evaluation/datasets/sources/vienna4x22` contains CC BY 4.0 score-performance
annotations and symbolic score artifacts from the Vienna 4x22 Piano Corpus by
Werner Goebl, with match-file updates by the Institute of Computational
Perception. Evaluation audio is not distributed in this Git repository.

The optional experimental BeatNet model pack uses the BeatNet ONNX model by
Mojtaba Heydari, Frank Cwitkowitz, and Zhiyao Duan under CC BY 4.0. Model files
are not distributed by this repository. The Rust frontend interoperates with
BeatNet's published feature contract and reimplements behavior from the
BSD-licensed madmom signal, STFT, logarithmic-filterbank, and spectrogram
difference modules. See `models/README.md` for pinned provenance and the
remaining training-corpus review requirement, and
`licenses/madmom-BSD-3-Clause.txt` for the retained source license terms.
